Package: pannet
Type: Package
Title: Neural Regression Models for Panel Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Imad", family = "El-Badisy", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "elbadisyimad@gmail.com")
Description: Implements neural regression models for panel and longitudinal data.
    The package provides multilayer perceptron architectures with pooled,
    individual-effect, time-effect, two-way-effect, and dynamic panel structures.
    Individual and time effects are learnable additive scalar embeddings initialised
    at zero and jointly optimised with the network weights. Supported outcome
    families include Gaussian (MSE), binomial (binary cross-entropy), Poisson
    (negative log-likelihood), multiclass (categorical cross-entropy), and
    fractional (quasi-binomial) outcomes. Training is performed natively via the
    torch package with no external learner dependency.
